spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r4.md:3:1. **High — Degraded mode still permits 
loss.** FR-001/033, AC-039 
([SPEC:125](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:125)). Unpersisted sends 
remain allowed. Closing the drawer or changing its view unmounts the composer without a browser unload warning; its 
text and key are component state 
([composer:133](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/message-composer.tsx:133), 
[drawer:279](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/MessagingDrawer.tsx:279)). This contradicts R1-q2 A 
and leaves r2 #1/r3 #2 open. **Fix:** “If persistence fails, do not dispatch; show an actionable storage failure and 
retain the composition.” AC-039 must assert zero create requests.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r4.md:7:3. **High — Notification authorization can 
return a stale positive result.** FR-025, BR-011, AC-049 
([SPEC:117](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:117)). Authorize B, hold 
the positive response, remove B while Realtime is blocked, then release it: the last completed check still says 
“member.” Holding the request before authorization does not test this race. Literal membership at browser emission 
cannot be guaranteed by a prior server read. **Fix:** define the authorization boundary explicitly, require final 
identity/revocation checks without intervening awaits, and obtain owner acceptance of any remaining check-to-display 
race. AC-049 must hold an already-positive response.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r4.md:13:6. **Medium — Polling cannot fulfill the 
promised outage read-state synchronization.** FR-016/021, AC-016/021 
([SPEC:108](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:108)). Polling fetches new 
messages and the list; receipts for existing messages and open reader details can remain stale. Reader details have a 
separate query, refreshed through receipt events/rejoin 
([readers:15](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/queries/useMessageReaders.ts:15)). **Fix:** include 
existing-message receipt summaries and open reader-detail queries in fallback reconciliation. Test partial reads 
during a Realtime-only outage without sending another message.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r4.md:17:8. **Medium — Expired manual retry has 
contradictory retry rules.** FR-008/009, BR-006, AC-010 
([SPEC:101](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:101)). After manual retry 
receives 429, FR-008 requires automatic retry, but the unchanged item remains older than 24 hours and FR-009 prohibits 
automatic sending. **Fix:** explicitly define a renewed delivery window upon manual retry, retaining the key and 
original timestamp for metrics. Test manual retry followed by 429 and an unknown outcome.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r4.md:27:10. **Medium — Old-build compatibility 
has no direct acceptance check.** §10, AC-033/034 
([SPEC:177](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:177)). Tests against the 
new handler cannot prove that the hosted old handler’s direct inserts survive new fencing requirements, grants, or 
required columns. The existing legacy path inserts directly ([repository:511](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/repositor
ies/implementations/supabase/SupabaseMessageRepository.ts:511)). **Fix:** define compatibility for unkeyed legacy 
writes and existing RPC signatures, then require the preserved old handler to run against the migrated local database 
before online application.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r4.md:29:11. **Low — The baseline description 
remains inaccurate.** §2 
([SPEC:13](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:13)) says only messages 
catch up. The conversation stream already invalidates the list after confirmed joins 
([subscription:58](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/realtime/useConversationRealtime.ts:58)). **Fix:** describe 
the missing terminal-closure recovery, aggregate health, and polling without claiming list catch-up is absent.
