spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r3.md:1:r2 findings remain open/partial: **#1, #2, 
#3 (J1 only), #5, #6, #13, #14**. Findings **#4, #7–#12, #15–#19** are resolved in v2. D1–D4 are accepted. All 32 Must 
FRs and 16 BRs have AC links; the semantic coverage gaps below remain.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r3.md:3:1. **High — FR-004–006/009, AC-041–042: 
absence does not prove safe cancellation or takeover.** A closed tab’s accepted create can remain blocked before 
INSERT. Lookup returns absent, another tab cancels/expires/resends, then the original create commits. The existing 
repository separates lookup from INSERT ([SupabaseMessageRepository.ts:530](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/repositorie
s/implementations/supabase/SupabaseMessageRepository.ts:530)). A live but hung owner can also block recovery 
indefinitely. [SPEC:96](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:96). **Fix:** 
require server-fenced attempt ownership and bounded recovery; unknown becomes waiting only when no previous attempt 
can still commit. Test with the original INSERT blocked in real Postgres through lookup, cancellation, and takeover. 
**r2 #2/#5 remain partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r3.md:5:2. **High — FR-001 versus §11/AC-039: 
IndexedDB failure bypasses durability.** The Phase 4 fallback permits dispatch without durable storage, reopening the 
original close-before-response loss window. Phase 4 keeps the key in a component ref and uses plain fetch 
([message-composer.tsx:145](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/message-composer.tsx:145), 
[messaging-api.ts:131](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging-api.ts:131)). 
[SPEC:196](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:196). **Fix:** “If the 
durable write fails, do not dispatch or clear the composer; retain the composition with an actionable storage 
failure.” AC-039 must inject storage failure with HTTP working and assert zero create requests. **r2 #1 remains 
partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r3.md:9:4. **Medium — FR-011, AC-012/013/044: late 
completions remain untested.** AC-044 pauses before dispatch; AC-013 stops drains but never releases a late 
success/error afterward. Existing completions write to conversation-only cache keys 
([useMessages.ts:317](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/useMessages.ts:317)). 
[SPEC:275](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:275). **Fix:** add E2Es 
releasing real create and lookup responses after A→C and confirmed logout. Assert no old content enters C’s view, no 
deleted item reappears, and stale completions cannot modify replacement claims. **r2 #6 remains partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r3.md:15:7. **Medium — FR-027/028, AC-028/029: 
metrics bounds regressed and hanging delivery is insufficiently bounded.** V1 explicitly bounded request size and 
batch length ([SPEC-v1-reviewed.md:205](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/reviews
/SPEC-v1-reviewed.md:205)); v2 retains only field bounds, a client buffer, and request-rate limiting. One enormous 
valid batch can flood logs. Repeated hanging batches can accumulate outside the buffer and consume HTTP capacity. 
[SPEC:119](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:119). **Fix:** restore 
byte/event-count limits; define bounded concurrent delivery, cancellation deadlines, and overload dropping. Test 
oversized valid batches and sustained hanging traffic while messaging continues. **r2 #14 remains partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r3.md:21:10. **Medium — FR-014–016, AC-015/016: 
independent health and non-degradation are not fully asserted.** AC-015 checks independent recovery, while AC-016 
tests a combined outage and only message uniqueness during overlap. These can pass with message-only banner/polling 
health or stale polling overwriting enriched state. Existing status exposes only the message channel 
([MessagingContext.tsx:251](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/contexts/messaging/MessagingContext.tsx:251)); raw events 
omit enrichment 
([useMessageSubscription.ts:48](/E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/realtime/useMessageSubscription.ts:48)). 
[SPEC:246](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:246). **Fix:** 
independently assert banner/polling thresholds for both required streams, and release stale polls after newer Realtime 
updates while checking attachments, mentions, reactions, receipts, and pagination. **r2 #13 remains partial.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-spec-r3.md:23:11. **Medium — FR-021/022 versus FR-016; 
J1 versus D1: deadlines conflict.** Five-second cross-device synchronization is unconditional, but Realtime-only 
failure permits no polling for 30 seconds and then 15-second intervals. J1 still promises every pending message within 
ten seconds without D1’s queue/quota conditions. 
[SPEC:77](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:77), 
[SPEC:113](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:113), 
[state.md:216](/E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/state.md:216). **Fix:** state 
healthy-connectivity prerequisites for the five-second target, cross-reference degraded deadlines, and copy D1’s 
qualification into J1. **r2 #3 remains open only in J1.**
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-plan-r3.md:1:**Verdict: approve.** All seven carried 
findings are resolved in [PLAN v3](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md). 
One new Low finding remains.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-plan-r3.md:6:| R8 — Split completion clauses | 
**Resolved** | T9 L147–148 verifies the original timestamp survives retry. T19 L228–229 now requires emitted latency 
to use it. T18’s replay notification check and T23’s application-first rollback remain present. |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-plan-r3.md:13:The fence definition preserves ordinary 
Phase 4 retry because generation-less creation creates no fence state. It also closes the late-insert race: 
generation-less **insertions** must participate in atomic fence exclusion, while generated attempts must pass their 
current-generation check. Stored-message replay remains governed by the explicit 200/409 compatibility requirement; it 
cannot be treated as a new insertion and blanket-rejected.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-plan-r3.md:15:The Phoenix boundary is compatible with 
[SPEC §15](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:299): faults enter through 
the transport while real joins, Supabase and application callbacks remain active. Playwright supports interception 
connected to the real server, and Phoenix defines channel-specific error/closure frames. This is single-stream 
protocol fault shaping under the stated constraints. [Playwright 
documentation](https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-websocketroute#web-socket-route-connect-to-server), [Supabase 
protocol](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/protocol#server-sent-events).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience\reviews\sol-review-plan-r3.md:17:T25’s native-status requirement prevents 
ordinary event dropping from masquerading as a subscription timeout. T27 now respects FR-009/BR-006 expiry; 
FR-005/BR-007’s unclaimed, atomic cancellation requirement remains owned by T10 L137–139.
