.planning\phases\02-floor-plan-completion\02-REVIEWS.md:24:I’ll review this as a plan-quality and regression-risk 
pass, with the presence/offline bug as the main lens. I’m using the `presence-safety` and `supabase` skills because 
the plans touch realtime presence, location APIs, and Supabase state boundaries.
.planning\phases\02-floor-plan-completion\02-REVIEWS.md:28:The plans are directionally strong and show good awareness 
of the major Phase 2 failure modes, especially after the gap-closure plans. The main weakness is that the plan set 
contains conflicting presence rules: early plans clear `current_space_id` on offline cleanup, while later 
reload-recovery logic depends on preserving it. That conflict, combined with insufficient explicit filtering of 
`status === 'offline'` users from `usersInSpaces`, is the most likely path to the observed ghost/offline users 
regression.
