   1: -- Phase 5 T1 / FR-029, FR-030, AC-030, AC-031
   2: -- (spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience): Phase 4 database follow-ups.
   3: --
   4: -- 1) mark_conversation_read(p_conversation_id, p_user_id) refuses non-members.
   5: --    It is SECURITY DEFINER and trusts p_user_id. Since 20261004170724 only
   6: --    service_role (and the owner) may EXECUTE it, but its body UPSERTED the
   7: --    membership row: a call for a user outside the conversation silently made
   8: --    them a member (conversation_members drives RLS on messages) and wrote read
   9: --    receipts on their behalf. The body now only UPDATEs an existing membership
  10: --    row and raises 42501 when there is none, so nothing is written for a
  11: --    non-member whatever role executes it (postgres/owner included). The UPDATE
  12: --    is the membership check itself: it holds the row lock until commit, so a
  13: --    concurrent membership removal cannot slip between check and receipts.
  14: --    Null arguments raise 22004 instead of failing on a NOT NULL constraint.
  15: --    search_path is now '' (every reference is schema-qualified, as in
  16: --    mark_messages_read).
  17: --
  18: -- 2) get_unread_counts(uuid[]) is no longer executable by anon. Migration
  19: --    20260610210000 revoked it from public and granted authenticated, but
  20: --    Supabase's default privileges for functions created by postgres in public
  21: --    (pg_default_acl: anon, authenticated, service_role = X) had already given
  22: --    anon EXECUTE. anon has no auth.uid(), so it only ever got an empty set;
  23: --    the grant is removed so the anon key cannot reach this SECURITY DEFINER
  24: --    function at all.
  25: --
  26: -- Backward compatible with the hosted pre-Phase-4 build and the Phase 4 build
  27: -- (SPEC section 10):
  28: --   * signatures, parameter names, return types, SECURITY DEFINER, and the
  29: --     write semantics for members (last_read_at = updated_at = now(), receipts
  30: --     for every message from others) are unchanged;
  31: --   * the only mark_conversation_read caller is
  32: --     SupabaseConversationRepository.markConversationRead on the service-role
  33: --     client in PATCH /api/conversations/read, which already 403s non-members
  34: --     via requireConversationParticipant (conversation_members, same check on
  35: --     main), so it never reaches the removed INSERT branch;
  36: --   * the only get_unread_counts caller is SupabaseConversationRepository
  37: --     .findByUser on the user-scoped client in GET /api/conversations/get,
  38: --     which runs only after requireAuthUser, i.e. as authenticated.
  39: --     authenticated and service_role keep EXECUTE.
  40: --
  41: -- Locking: CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION and GRANT/REVOKE only touch catalog rows
  42: -- (brief locks; in-flight calls finish on the old body). lock_timeout makes the
  43: -- migration fail fast instead of queueing; re-run it when that happens.
  44: -- Transactional and re-runnable (CREATE OR REPLACE, idempotent GRANT/REVOKE).
  45: --
  46: -- Rollback restores the pre-migration body as written in 20260610210000
  47: -- (logically identical to the pre-migration catalog body; only line endings
  48: -- may differ), its absent comment, and the pre-migration ACLs. It REOPENS the
